    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0172" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">492.119/11–1050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Thailand
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d84-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-11-10T17:00:00-05:00">November 10,
                            1950—5 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>481. From Commerce: Current deterioration of French position in Indochina focuses
                    attention upon adequacy of United States export controls with respect to
                    Indochina and Thailand. Your vigilance as indicated your message<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d84-f2"/> regarding local controls, end use and consignee
                    information regarding some proposed shipments and extent of reexports and
                    smuggling strategic goods is appreciated. However, Commerce feels need for
                    restating its obligation and concern regarding <pb facs="0173" n="159"
                        xml:id="pg159"/> final disposition United States strategic goods going to
                    these areas and urges continuation and intensification your attention to efforts
                    Commies obtaining strategic goods via transshipment and smuggling and reporting
                    development for formulation policy and procedure changes here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d84-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d84-f1-content">
